From 47071154b380820ebbd22a6083c4f45bbca5d376 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daurosk <354202035+daurosk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:38:47 -0900
Subject: [PATCH] Co-op texture overrides: a module may have a texture drawn
 with other texels

host/hos_coop_texture.h, host/coop_texture.c: the exe keeps the textures
the game makes (nvnTextureInitialize to nvnTextureFinalize, told by
nvn_native.c) and a co-op module's overrides on their storage. Two
exports, found by name: hos_coop_textures (the textures of a storage
size, with a generation number) and hos_coop_texture_override (bytes
read in place of a texture's guest memory; NULL takes them away). The
renderers read a texture's storage through hos_coop_texture_overlay:
the Vulkan one in guest_bytes (every CPU and ASTC upload path; a
texture with an override skips the GPU unswizzle and the all-zero
clear), the WebGPU one in decode. Guest memory is never written: an
override set or taken away marks its pages written, so the texture is
uploaded again. A texture finalized takes its overrides with it.
The Link customizer paints Link's gear with it.
---
 gpu/render/rx_texture.cpp |   8 ++
 gpu/vk/vk_texture.cpp     |  55 ++++++++++-
 host/coop_texture.c       | 190 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 host/hos_coop_texture.h   |  43 +++++++++
 host/nvn_native.c         |   9 ++
 5 files changed, 301 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 host/coop_texture.c
 create mode 100644 host/hos_coop_texture.h

